    {
      "id": "clc-features-each-feature-script-executes-as-its-own-layer-to-desc-6a08d1b6",
      "clause": "clu-features-each-feature-script-executes-as-its-own-layer-to-desc-6a08d1b6",
      "disposition": "non-testable",
      "rationale": "An implementation note about build layering as a caching aid. The spec admits any strategy that installs the Features, deacon's layering is reported on no channel, and the outcome that matters — each Feature present in the resulting image — is claimed by bhv-up-feature-install-order and bhv-build-features-extended-image."
    },
    {
      "id": "clc-features-feature-identifiers-should-be-assumed-to-be-case-desc-68ef18bd",
      "clause": "clu-features-feature-identifiers-should-be-assumed-to-be-case-desc-68ef18bd",
      "disposition": "non-testable",
      "rationale": "Case-insensitive identifiers normalized to lowercase. The identifiers in question are OCI repository references, which the registry API already constrains to lowercase, so a mixed-case reference does not resolve at all rather than resolving differently; no reachable configuration makes the normalization separately observable."
    },
    {
      "id": "clc-features-feature-scripts-run-as-the-root-user-and-sometim-desc-86913dfe",
      "clause": "clu-features-feature-scripts-run-as-the-root-user-and-sometim-desc-86913dfe",
      "disposition": "non-testable",
      "rationale": "The motivating sentence for the `_REMOTE_USER`/`_CONTAINER_USER` variables: scripts run as root and therefore need to be told which account the container will be used with. Both halves are carried by other clauses of this same section — the root execution by the `install.sh` invocation clause, the variables by the three clauses that name them — each mapped on its own. A motivation sentence has nothing separately observable."
    },
